def find_sup_f_t_over_t(f_function, num_pieces_K, limit_at_infinity):
    max_ratio = limit_at_infinity

    # Assume f_function provides access to its linear pieces' endpoints
    for piece_start_t, piece_end_t in f_function.get_piece_endpoints():
        if piece_start_t > 0:
            max_ratio = max(max_ratio, f_function(piece_start_t) / piece_start_t)
        if piece_end_t > 0:
            max_ratio = max(max_ratio, f_function(piece_end_t) / piece_end_t)

    return max_ratio

formal_description.statement:
Let epsilon >= 0 and lambda_T_approx be such that lambda_T / (1 + epsilon) <= lambda_T_approx <= lambda_T. Assume that T is feasible on a sufficiently large number of unit-speed processors. Then:
(i) if lambda_T_approx > m, T is infeasible on m unit speed processors;
(ii) if lambda_T_approx <= m, T is EDF-schedulable on m speed-(2 - 1/m + epsilon) processors and DM-schedulable on m speed-(3 - 1/m + epsilon) processors.

